    </div>

    // Rest of the component...
  );
});
```

3. Repeat step 2 for all other HTML elements that need an ID.

Adding IDs can make it easier to select and manipulate elements using JavaScript or CSS. It also helps with accessibility, as screen readers and keyboard navigation rely on unique IDs to identify and navigate through different elements on the page. However, be careful not to overuse IDs, as having too many can make your HTML less scalable and more difficult to maintain. Use them sparingly and only when necessary.

